Completed ATAC-seq open-chromatin workflow in Galaxy history bbd44e69cb8906b568d7f4c11366ac19.

Steps:
- Created paired collection raw_pe_pair_for_fastp (c81e04c82691f815) from the provided forward/reverse FASTQ datasets.
- Ran fastp 1.3.6+galaxy0 in paired mode with paired-end adapter detection/overlap trimming, Q20 low-quality threshold, 70 percent unqualified limit, and minimum post-trim length 15.
- Aligned trimmed pairs with Bowtie2 2.5.5+galaxy0 to built-in hg19.
- Filtered alignments with Samtools view expression: flag.proper_pair == 2 && mapq >= 30 && rname != "chrM".
- Coordinate-sorted filtered BAM, then removed PCR duplicates with Picard MarkDuplicates remove_duplicates=true.
- Called peaks with MACS2 2.2.9.1+galaxy0 using BAMPE, q-value 0.05, no control, and keep-dup all.
- Exported first three columns from MACS2 narrowPeaks to final_answer/peaks.bed.
